  "terminal_budget_cases": [
    "Cancellation and original deadline interrupt five-second backoff in under one second, keep one initial execution, release byte budget and allow a follow-up under max_concurrent_rpcs(1).",
    "An oversized request with RESOURCE_EXHAUSTED configured as retryable returns locally, records no call/attempt and no server execution. A subsequent eligible failure can retry in a maxTokens=2 bucket, proving the encode rejection did not debit throttling.",
    "Client-streaming and bidi with retry policy each send request DATA, execute once, then return UNAVAILABLE after RST_STREAM(CANCEL). Zero policy retries, zero retained byte budget and successful follow-up under one-RPC admission."
  ],
  "limits": [
    "Unknown means a peer records the execution and drops its TCP connection before response headers. It is returned as UNAVAILABLE unless explicit policy authorizes another counted attempt; the test does not assert exactly-once execution.",
    "Fixed seeds 0..15 include deterministic boundary scripts plus xorshift-generated combinations; this is a bounded history corpus, not a model checker or long-running soak.",
    "QG-15 still owns routing-load guard retention across backoff. QG-16 owns policy_retries incrementing on a decision before a subsequent attempt is dispatched; the backoff tests currently use that decision counter as their readiness signal.",
    "Full workspace 3232-test and 46-case native/Go interop qualification was recorded for the unchanged transport implementation in encoded-request-replay.json. This tests-only follow-up does not claim a new full workspace/interop run or full release/performance qualification."
  ]
}
